{"issue": true, "summary": "The `map` function in pLimit can leave orphaned promise rejections when the iterable contains rejected promises, because the `enqueue` function doesn't properly handle rejections from the mapped functions before they are queued.", "edits": [{"path": "index.js", "old": "return Promise.all(promises);", "new": "return Promise.all(promises).catch(error => {
		// If any promise in the map fails, we need to ensure that
		// the queue is cleared to prevent orphaned rejections.
		if (rejectOnClear) {
			generator.clearQueue();
		}
		throw error;
	});"}]}
